From 86be5230001faeed3908dce4d8428955e2c47dec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:40:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(distributed): rank-order reduce-scatter in
 batch-invariant mode

NCCL adds the ranks' partials of a reduce-scatter chunk in an order that
depends on the receiving rank and the message size, so under DeepSeek
V4.1 prefill sequence parallelism a row's bits change with the batch's
row count and the row's position. With VLLM_DS41_BATCH_INVARIANT=1 the
TP reduce-scatter exchanges the chunks (grouped send/recv on the same
communicator, the same bytes) and adds them locally in rank order.
